  "synthesis": {
    "description": "Risk keeps the list of Enovate/EMW and other trading books that must be officialized each night, since Credit picks up all officialized books. When a book is missed or the list is wrong, Darron Giron explains why the benchmark signoff did not catch it, updates the list and recirculates it, sometimes after misreading what was asked.",
    "steps": [
      "A request arrives for the current list of books officialized each night.",
      "The list of books is compiled and checked against the books in use.",
      "Books are marked official so Credit and downstream users pick them up.",
      "Missed books or errors are explained and the list is corrected and resent."
    ],
    "approach": "Maintain the officialized book list as a controlled list in the risk system and run a nightly check that compares books marked official against that list, reporting any book left unofficialized before Credit picks them up.",
    "rationale": "The failures are missed books and lists that drift out of date; a nightly checklist tied to a maintained book list catches misses before they reach downstream users.",
    "artifact_type": "checklist"
  },
